; lib/core, rebuilt for Melange. Same copy-never-fork rule as the walk_core
; mirror.
;
; No hand-written entry module is needed here: lib/core's own core.ml IS the
; module consumers name, so [wrapped false] already yields [Core].
;
; The error framework it used to hold is now [Err], mirrored separately by
; js/melange/vendor/err_trace; what remains here is [Core.Pretty].
;
; [Err.fail] captures a callstack through [Printexc.get_callstack]. Melange
; declares it, but at runtime it yields a value its own [raw_backtrace_length]
; cannot read -- the emitted code is [bt.length] and the value is [undefined].
; [Err.Stack] therefore asks [Printexc.backtrace_slots], which Melange converts
; defensively and answers [None] for, the same fallback js_of_ocaml takes. No
; shim is required; the probe just must not print anything that differs between
; the two branches.

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/lib/core/*.{ml,mli}))

(library
 (name core_mel)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes melange)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{profile} melange))
 (libraries fmt_mel err_trace_mel))
